{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/54","id":4686936303,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF1z47w","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/54","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/54.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/54.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/54","number":54,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"research(30002061): reviewed relative-collapse reduction and planar certificates","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Partial result; original Hudson problem remains unsolved\n\nThis package preserves the exact source's linear-subdivision and prescribed-target conditions. It gives an elementary equivalence with the protected-boundary problem for one subdivided simplex, and reconstructs a constructive relative-collapse certificate in dimensions at most two. These are credited low-dimensional/reduction facts, with no novelty claim.\n\nThe general higher-dimensional problem is not solved. The dual-tree method leaves a higher-dimensional contractible residual for which no relative free-face sequence is supplied. Adiprasito–Benedetti's published theorem adds a barycentric subdivision to both complexes; it is credited and not substituted for the original target. A general PL ball or a nonshellable triangulation is not asserted to be a counterexample.\n\n## Independent review and exact certificates\n\nA separate adversarial review passed the frozen partial result, with no required mathematical corrections. The author checker passes 4,200 exact rational/face-set assertions over 27 disk meshes and six gluing controls. Independent verification passes 59,718 invariant assertions over 387 disk-target cases, 387 external-gluing cases and 30 interval cases. Counts include repeated invariants at successive moves; these are not high-dimensional search results.\n\nAn explicit small certificate and both review receipts are included. Run `python3 unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30002061/verify.py` with the Python standard library.\n\nActual model: gpt-6-astra, xhigh. One substantive family, stopped at the precise relative-collapse gap. Recommended queue status: unsolved, 1/5. The coordinator owns queue edits.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:48:31Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:53:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"feaafe4c07fa2ce1db7de671b2ab68854a2f5840","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/54/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/54/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/54/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/28c6ce952d6027fb995bbd2d79a8c9647cc8b844","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-30002061","ref":"dot/math-3000206